{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto"]]},"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/proceed()"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/gnusto\/proceed()"]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Writing Rules","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WritingRules","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Rule","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Rules","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Intent","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Command","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/say(_:)","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/sayOnceThisTurn(_:)","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/say(_:from:)-9dkx0","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/say(_:from:)-29lpm","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/say(_:from:)-9dafx","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/say(_:from:)-1kn0c","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Earshot","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/refuse(_:)","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/reply(_:)","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/require(_:else:)"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Writing-Rules"}],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"proceed","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"}],"modules":[{"name":"Gnusto"}],"title":"proceed()","symbolKind":"func","externalID":"s:6Gnusto7proceedyyKF","roleHeading":"Function","role":"symbol"},"abstract":[{"text":"Runs the stage-4 default action (a game\/plugin override if one is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"registered for this intent, else the built-in) immediately, then returns","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so the calling rule can embellish the result — print something more, read","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"state the default action changed, and so on.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"proceed","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"mentions","mentions":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WritingRules"]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Callable from any stage 1–3 "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"before"},{"type":"text","text":"-phase rule — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"world.before"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"location.beforeEachTurn"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"location.before"},{"type":"text","text":", or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"item.before"},{"type":"text","text":", on either"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the indirect or direct object — and only once per turn. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"proceed()"},{"type":"text","text":" means"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"“run the default now; I take responsibility”: once it runs, the pipeline"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"skips its own stage-4 step (so the default doesn’t run twice) "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"and","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"skips every remaining before rule still ahead of the calling rule in this"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"turn’s sequence — including later rules in the same before-phase, not just"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"later phases. A guard written as a later "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"before"},{"type":"text","text":" rule — whether a sibling"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in the same phase or an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"item.before"},{"type":"text","text":" rule on the direct object when"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"proceed()"},{"type":"text","text":" was called from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"world.before"},{"type":"text","text":" — never gets to run, so it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can’t refuse an action that has already happened. Calling it from an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"after"},{"type":"text","text":"\/each-turn"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rule, or calling it twice, is a programmer error and traps with a clear"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"message rather than silently double-running the default action."}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["mailbox.before(.open) {","    try proceed()                    \/\/ built-in open runs here","    say(\"A city map is tucked inside the lid.\")","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If the default action throws (e.g. a built-in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"open"},{"type":"text","text":" refuses because the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"item is locked), that "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TurnInterrupt"},{"type":"text","text":" propagates out of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"proceed()"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"exactly as it would have out of the pipeline’s own stage 4."}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/reply(_:)":{"role":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/reply(_:)","title":"reply(_:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Fully handles the current action with a response, skipping the default"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"behavior. Mechanically identical to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refuse(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" — two names exist so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"game code rea